1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:06,967
Hanoi, French colonial Vietnam.

2
00:00:06,967 --> 00:00:08,627
The French built new sewers

3
00:00:08,627 --> 00:00:10,845
under their part of town.

4
00:00:10,845 --> 00:00:12,505
Rats loved them.

5
00:00:12,505 --> 00:00:13,863
They came up through the toilets,

6
00:00:13,863 --> 00:00:16,669
and plague was spreading across Asia.

7
00:00:16,919 --> 00:00:18,986
So in April 1902 the city

8
00:00:18,986 --> 00:00:20,820
opened a hunt for everyone:

9
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:23,119
bring in a rat tail, get paid —

10
00:00:23,119 --> 00:00:27,449
reportedly one cent a tail. Just the tail.

11
00:00:27,449 --> 00:00:28,935
Nobody wanted piles of dead

12
00:00:28,935 --> 00:00:30,597
rats at the police station.

13
00:00:30,847 --> 00:00:34,713
It worked... on paper. At the peak,

14
00:00:34,713 --> 00:00:36,547
over 20,000 tails

15
00:00:36,547 --> 00:00:38,295
came in a single day.

16
00:00:38,545 --> 00:00:40,379
Then officials started seeing

17
00:00:40,379 --> 00:00:43,026
rats running around with no tails.

18
00:00:43,026 --> 00:00:45,023
People had figured it out:

19
00:00:45,023 --> 00:00:47,311
cut off the tail, let the rat go,

20
00:00:47,311 --> 00:00:52,071
let it make more rats — and more tails.

21
00:00:52,071 --> 00:00:53,766
Inspectors even found rat

22
00:00:53,766 --> 00:00:55,413
farms outside the city.

23
00:00:55,663 --> 00:00:57,648
The city wanted fewer rats.

24
00:00:57,648 --> 00:01:00,864
It paid for tails. So it got tails.

25
00:01:00,864 --> 00:01:01,700
The hunt failed,

26
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:03,709
and the plague came anyway.

27
00:01:03,709 --> 00:01:05,439
Historian Michael Vann,

28
00:01:05,439 --> 00:01:06,565
who dug the story out

29
00:01:06,565 --> 00:01:07,784
of the colonial archives,

30
00:01:07,784 --> 00:01:11,268
calls it "absolutely a disaster."
